Higher `kw` favours queries that name their subject; lower favours ones
that describe it. `floor` is the cosine under which a vector match counts
for nothing — and because a hit scoring zero relevance is skipped rather
than ranked last, the floor is a delete, not a demotion. A query that
names nothing scores zero on keywords too, so it is the one phrasing that
can trip both conditions at once and vanish before the reranker sees it.
There is no optimum here independent of how often each phrasing happens —
which is the assumption printed above, not a measurement.
